  "notes": [
    "Auxiliary group prices accumulate source-ordered filled amounts and costs, exclude the initial fill, and reset at the source group/global exits.",
    "The source group exit anchor takes precedence over the latest level-four de-risk anchor, including after later de-risk orders.",
    "Buyback de-risk uses the actual trade close fee in group profit; the Futures capture configures a distinct virtual close fee.",
    "Partial-exit tags retain the active group entry IDs in reverse source order. Re-entry follows the new exit anchor.",
    "The source mode guards remain in the action programs. Source system_v4 fixes derisk_4_enable=False; the zero-buyback capture does not establish active v4 buyback execution.",
    "Donor callbacks and class constants remain unchanged; signal and indicator transformations are disclosed in sealed recipes."
  ],
